<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεῖψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>omission</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἄρθρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					78.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>failure, lack</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
					8(1).182
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Math.,
				<i>negative term</i> in an algebraic expression, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαρξις, λ. ἐπὶ λεῖψιν πολλαπλασιασθεῖσα
				ποιεῖ ὕπαρξιν</span>
			<i>a minus</i> multiplied by <i>a minus</i> gives a plus, <i><span class="en">
				Dioph.
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Def.</u>
				9
			</span></i>: dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείψει</span> c. gen.,
				<i>minus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.21
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
